\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Proposed Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL follows the Single Authority Principle. Every durable piece of system state has exactly one authoritative owner. Only the owning service may mutate that state. All other services interact with it through commands and queries, and may maintain read-only projections or caches that are explicitly treated as non-authoritative.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
