\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Most software systems have architecture...\
...but the software itself doesn't know it.\
Humans know.\
Diagrams know.\
Documentation knows.\
The application does not.\
So if you ask Kubernetes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Why are you deploying this pod?"\strokec2 \
It can't really answer.\
If you ask a web application:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Draw your architecture."\strokec2 \
It can't.\
HAL is different.\
HAL is an intelligence.\
So...\
Should HAL understand itself?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

