\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. My recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Option D. Strong recommendation\'979.8/10 confidence.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
A capability should be a 
\f0\b \strokec2 durable, implementation-independent contract for achieving an outcome
\f1\b0 \strokec2 .\
This is the right architecture because it preserves the distinction we have repeatedly established:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Identity is not execution.\strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \strokec2 Authority is not compute.\strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \strokec2 Capability is not implementation.\strokec2 \
HAL should reason in capabilities.\
Nodes, models, services, and tools should register as providers of those capabilities.\
For example, the user asks:\
