\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed locked decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall represent its functional abilities as implementation-independent Capability Contracts. A capability defines a meaningful outcome, its accepted inputs, expected outputs, constraints, quality requirements, permissions, risk classification, side effects, and evaluation criteria.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Models, tools, services, nodes, humans, and workflows may act as Capability Providers. Providers shall declare the conditions under which they can satisfy a capability and shall be evaluated using observed evidence, including quality, reliability, latency, cost, privacy, resource requirements, and known limitations.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall resolve capability requests into execution plans through the Decision Engine. Users and higher-level workflows shall depend on capability contracts rather than specific providers or implementations. Capabilities may be composed into higher-order capabilities, enabling HAL to generate, compare, execute, and evaluate alternative plans without coupling intent to infrastructure.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Capability contracts shall classify external effects and risk so that authorization, confirmation, autonomy, auditing, retry, rollback, and compensation behavior can be governed consistently.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
That is my recommendation for Decision 10.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
