\cf0 \strokec2 I think there's an even more general statement underneath all of these:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 HAL separates concepts from implementations.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
That's actually what we've been doing all along.\
The Constitution is independent of who enforces it.\
Capabilities are independent of who provides them.\
Objectives are independent of how they're executed.\
Identity is independent of display names.\
Authority is independent of compute.\
That separation is one of the reasons I think HAL will be able to evolve for years without requiring architectural rewrites.\
