\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. My Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Recommendation: 10/10 confidence.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
I think Option C is the inevitable destination for HAL.\
Not because "knowledge graphs are cool."\
Because it aligns with everything we've already locked.\
The Self Model becomes a subgraph.\
The World Model becomes a subgraph.\
Objectives become subgraphs.\
Capabilities become subgraphs.\
Decision history links to the objectives it influenced, the providers it selected, the evidence it considered, and the outcomes it produced.\
Nothing is isolated anymore.\
Everything is connected through meaning.\
That means HAL doesn't just retrieve information\'97it can 
\f2\i \strokec2 reason across domains
\f1\i0 \strokec2 .\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Show me every infrastructure decision influenced by my preference for local-first execution."\strokec2 \
Or:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Which capabilities became available after adding GX10-07, and which objectives benefited from them?"\strokec2 \
Those aren't bespoke queries. They're traversals through a unified model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

