\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall maintain a unified Knowledge Graph composed of typed entities and explicit relationships. The Knowledge Graph represents HAL's evolving understanding of itself, the external world, objectives, capabilities, providers, decisions, policies, and all other operational domains. Each entity type maintains domain-specific attributes while participating in a common relationship model.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 The immutable Conversation Archive remains the authoritative historical record. The Knowledge Graph is a derived, evolving representation built from archived evidence, observations, and reasoning. HAL shall reason across the Knowledge Graph rather than isolated subsystem data models, enabling explainable, cross-domain understanding and future extensibility.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
This is one of the few decisions where my confidence is an unqualified 
\f0\b \strokec2 10/10
\f1\b0 \strokec2 . If I were designing HAL from scratch with the benefit of everything we've learned so far, this is the foundation I would choose every time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Option C feels like the only truly viable option. Let's lock it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 I agree completely.\
