\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall employ a Hierarchical Adaptive Planning Architecture. Objectives are decomposed through progressively more concrete layers: Strategy, Milestones, Plans, Tasks, Capability Requests, and Provider Execution. Each layer has a distinct responsibility and may be independently evaluated, modified, or replanned without invalidating higher-level intent. HAL shall reuse proven planning patterns where appropriate while retaining the ability to generate, compare, and adapt plans dynamically based on evidence, changing conditions, and observed outcomes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
This is another decision where my confidence is extremely high. It doesn't just solve planning\'97it creates the operational bridge between everything we've already designed and the distributed execution layer we'll eventually build. I think this is the natural next pillar for HAL.\
