\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 6. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall maintain an Operational Provider Registry representing the providers currently available for execution. Providers may be discovered through environment inspection, connector installation, explicit user definition, administrative configuration, or other discovery mechanisms. HAL owns the provider model and shall not depend solely on provider self-registration.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Each provider maintains operational metadata including identity, availability, authentication, health, capability claims, observed capabilities, trust, benchmarks, licensing, policies, dependencies, and user preferences. Provider state evolves through the lifecycle of Known, Available, Verified, Preferred, Deprecated, and Retired. Changes to provider state generate operational events that inform planning, scheduling, trust evaluation, and execution.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 The Operational Provider Registry represents HAL's current execution environment and remains distinct from the Ecosystem Intelligence Model, which represents the broader external technology landscape.
