\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall represent capabilities as composable contracts within a Capability Graph. Capabilities define semantic inputs, outputs, preconditions, postconditions, quality expectations, authorization requirements, privacy constraints, side effects, failure semantics, and operational characteristics. HAL shall compose capabilities dynamically to achieve user outcomes rather than relying on fixed workflows.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL may maintain reusable Recipes representing proven patterns of capability composition. Recipes are advisory planning knowledge rather than executable workflows. They provide starting points for planning and may be adapted, extended, or partially applied based on user intent, context, available providers, evidence, and policy.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Provider selection occurs independently from capability composition, allowing capabilities to remain implementation-independent while enabling dynamic substitution, optimization, parallel execution, and continuous learning.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
