\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 6. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall define a Node as an independently schedulable execution environment. A Node is not synonymous with a physical machine, operating system process, container, or virtual machine. Instead, it represents the smallest execution environment to which HAL may independently allocate work.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 A single physical machine may host multiple Nodes, and a Node may represent physical, virtual, containerized, cloud, edge, or specialized execution environments. Physical hardware is modeled separately as resources owned or exposed by Nodes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Each Node shall authoritatively report its current operational state, including available resources, health, policies, operational limits, and environmental characteristics. HAL owns scheduling, orchestration, trust evaluation, and provider selection, while Nodes remain authoritative only for reporting their own observable execution environment.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Execution is allocated to Nodes based on their reported operational state and HAL's decision-making framework, preserving the separation between infrastructure description and execution authority.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
