\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall maintain a typed and extensible Resource Graph representing the physical, virtual, consumable, renewable, exclusive, shareable, partitionable, and externally metered resources available to its execution environment. Resources shall possess immutable identities, typed attributes, capacities, operational state, constraints, and explicit topology relationships.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall distinguish installed capacity, policy-allocatable capacity, reserved capacity, and currently available capacity. These values shall remain semantically separate and shall not be treated as interchangeable.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Capabilities and providers shall express execution requirements as abstract resource constraints rather than machine-specific bindings. Requirements shall distinguish mandatory constraints from optimization preferences. The Execution Orchestrator may optimize among preferences but shall never violate mandatory resource, privacy, security, or policy constraints.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall allocate resources through explicit, durable reservations associated with execution attempts. Reservations shall define quantity, exclusivity, priority, duration, expiration, preemption behavior, and ownership. Lease-based expiration shall prevent abandoned work from permanently retaining resources.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Nodes and resource agents shall be authoritative for reporting directly observable live resource state. HAL shall remain authoritative for trust, allocatable limits, reservations, priorities, placement, and interpretation of reported state.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 The Resource Graph shall represent topology, locality, dependency, partitioning, and shared contention so that logically distinct Nodes cannot cause HAL to treat shared underlying resources as independent capacity.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

