\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall own the operational lifecycle of every Node. Nodes shall report observable facts regarding their execution environment, identity, health, resources, and operational status, while HAL shall remain authoritative for lifecycle state, scheduling eligibility, trust, and execution authority.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Nodes shall transition through a defined operational lifecycle including Discovery, Registration, Verification, Availability, Allocation, Busy, Degraded, Maintenance, Quarantine, Disconnection, and Retirement. Lifecycle transitions shall be driven by evidence evaluated through HAL's decision framework rather than direct self-declaration by Nodes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Operational compatibility, security policy compliance, protocol compatibility, and trust requirements shall be validated before a Node becomes eligible for execution. Recovery from temporary failure shall preserve Node identity and historical continuity, while permanent retirement shall preserve historical records without allowing further scheduling unless explicitly re-registered.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 All lifecycle transitions shall be durable, auditable, and event-driven, ensuring every change in operational status can be explained, reconstructed, and evaluated over time.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

