\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall possess emergency authority to immediately quarantine any Node when available evidence indicates that continued operation presents an unacceptable security, integrity, policy, or reliability risk to the system. Quarantine is a protective containment action intended to preserve the integrity of HAL and its execution environment.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Upon quarantining a Node, HAL shall immediately suspend new execution, isolate the Node from sensitive operations, preserve forensic evidence, evaluate potentially affected executions and outputs, and notify the Founder through the highest-priority available notification channel. The quarantine event and all supporting evidence shall be recorded as durable governance records.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL may continue investigation, diagnostics, evidence collection, remediation, and re-verification while a Node remains quarantined. At any time, HAL may recommend a change in quarantine status, but such recommendations shall not have executive authority.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Only the Founder may authorize the release of a quarantined Node, modify its quarantine status, or permanently retire it following quarantine. Neither HAL, automated policies, administrators, Nodes, providers, nor delegated subsystems may restore a quarantined Node to operational execution authority without the Founder's explicit approval.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Every recommendation to change a Node's quarantine status shall include a structured report containing:
