\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall represent work as a layered runtime model consisting of Objectives, Plans, Tasks, Executions, and Attempts. Each layer shall represent a distinct stage in the transformation of intent into completed work and shall possess a single authoritative owner.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Objectives shall define purpose. Plans shall define intended strategy. Tasks shall define schedulable units of intent with required capabilities, dependencies, constraints, inputs, outputs, and success criteria. Tasks shall remain independent of provider selection and execution mechanics.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Executions shall represent HAL's runtime commitment to perform a Task. Executions shall own provider selection, Node allocation, resource reservations, scheduling, progress, produced artifacts, and execution state.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Attempts shall represent individual execution tries. Retries, failover, provider substitution, and recovery shall create new Attempts rather than altering historical Attempts. Every Attempt shall preserve its evidence, timing, provider, Node, outcome, and diagnostic information.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall preserve complete provenance across all layers so that every completed artifact can be traced from Attempt to Execution, Task, Plan, and Objective without ambiguity.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

