\fs36 \cf0 Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall represent work as a layered runtime model consisting of Objectives, Plans, Tasks, Executions, and Attempts. Each layer shall represent a distinct stage in the transformation of human intent into completed work and shall possess a single authoritative owner.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Objectives shall define purpose. Plans shall define the intended strategy. Tasks shall define schedulable units of intent, including required capabilities, dependencies, constraints, inputs, expected outputs, and success criteria. Tasks shall remain implementation-independent and shall not contain provider or infrastructure bindings.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Executions shall represent HAL's runtime commitment to perform a Task. Executions shall own provider selection, Node allocation, resource reservations, scheduling, runtime state, progress tracking, artifact production, and execution coordination.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Attempts shall represent individual execution tries. Retries, failover, provider substitution, execution migration, and recovery shall create new Attempts rather than modifying historical Attempts. Every Attempt shall preserve immutable evidence including timing, provider, Node, resource allocation, outcome, diagnostics, and produced artifacts where applicable.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall maintain complete provenance across all work layers so that every artifact, decision, execution, and outcome can be traced unambiguously from Attempt to Execution, Task, Plan, and Objective. Historical records shall remain immutable while higher layers continue to evolve through versioned planning and execution.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
