\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall use policy-constrained, multi-objective scheduling to determine when, where, and through which operational resources an Execution shall proceed. The Execution Orchestrator shall remain authoritative for scheduling, placement, reservation, dispatch, preemption, and admission control. Nodes and Providers may report operational evidence and limitations but shall not possess placement authority.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Scheduling shall occur in ordered stages: eligibility determination, feasibility validation, policy enforcement, candidate evaluation, resource reservation, and dispatch. Candidates that violate mandatory capability, resource, security, privacy, trust, cost, locality, authorization, or governance constraints shall be rejected before optimization occurs.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Among valid candidates, HAL shall evaluate explicit optimization dimensions including expected quality, completion time, reliability, monetary cost, resource efficiency, energy impact, data movement, interruption cost, provider trust, and reversibility. HAL may use internal scoring mechanisms, but consequential scheduling decisions shall preserve the material factors, tradeoffs, rejected alternatives, and rationale.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Scheduling priority shall be derived from semantically defined policy classes rather than an unexplained numerical score alone. Safety and containment shall take precedence, followed by explicitly authorized urgent work, interactive work, deadline-bound work, normal Objective work, maintenance, and speculative activity unless superseded by Founder policy.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall implement starvation prevention and policy-governed fairness across eligible work while preserving absolute safety, privacy, authorization, and governance constraints. Waiting time may strengthen a workload\'92s scheduling claim but shall not grant authority to violate a higher-order constraint.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL may preempt, pause, migrate, cancel, or defer execution only after evaluating priority, checkpointability, side effects, restart cost, progress, deadline impact, and system risk. Historical Attempts shall remain immutable, and every interruption or scheduling transition shall be durably recorded.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall perform admission control and may queue, defer, or reject work when immediate execution would violate commitments, exhaust protected capacity, endanger system stability, or prevent emergency operation.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

