\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall implement an evidence-based resilience model in which failure, partial completion, and uncertainty are represented as explicit operational states rather than being hidden by retries or overwritten by later outcomes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall distinguish failure at the Attempt, Execution, Task, Plan, and Objective layers. Failure at one layer shall not automatically imply failure at a higher layer. Recovery authority shall remain with the subsystem that owns the affected layer.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Attempts shall terminate with semantically explicit outcomes, including success, confirmed failure, timeout, cancellation, partial completion, and unknown outcome. Absence of confirmation shall not be interpreted as proof that an external effect did not occur.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Every executable operation shall declare its side-effect semantics, including whether it is pure, idempotent, compensatable, or irreversible and externally consequential. HAL shall permit automatic retry only when supported by those semantics, current evidence, and governing policy. Irreversible operations with uncertain outcomes shall not be blindly retried.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Recovery behavior shall be governed by explicit retry and recovery policies incorporating failure classification, idempotency, deadlines, cost, resource use, trust, operational health, and expected value. Every Execution shall possess bounded recovery budgets, and HAL shall stop retrying when further attempts are unjustified by evidence, policy, cost, or risk.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Long-running Executions should create durable, integrity-verified checkpoints where practical. Checkpoint compatibility and portability shall be established rather than assumed.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Attempt execution authority shall be lease-bound and protected through fencing, idempotency identities, or equivalent authoritative commit controls. Expired or superseded workers shall not be permitted to commit authoritative results, although late outputs shall remain preserved as evidence.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Attempt output shall be treated as a candidate result until accepted through an authoritative Execution commit. Result commitment shall validate current authority, provenance, integrity, success criteria, policy, and competing outcomes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall preserve explicit distinctions among full success, qualified success, partial satisfaction, blockage, and failure. It shall not represent incomplete work as complete or conceal unresolved uncertainty.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 When safe automated recovery is unavailable, exhausted, materially uncertain, or requires a change in intent, HAL shall escalate with the known evidence, unresolved uncertainty, available options, risks, recommendation, and calibrated confidence.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

