\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall communicate through four semantically distinct primitives: Commands, Queries, Events, and Streams. Communication semantics shall be determined by the intent of the interaction rather than by implementation technology or transport protocol.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Commands shall request authoritative state changes from a single authority. Queries shall retrieve authoritative state without producing side effects. Events shall represent immutable historical facts resulting from completed authoritative actions and shall remain durable, replayable, and ordered within their authority scope. Streams shall represent continuously changing operational observations whose value lies in current state rather than durable historical permanence.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall preserve strict semantic separation among these primitives. Commands shall never masquerade as Events, Queries shall never alter authoritative state, Events shall never request future work, and Streams shall never be interpreted as durable business facts unless explicitly transformed into authoritative Events through a defined decision process.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Subsystem contracts shall remain transport-independent. Communication semantics shall remain identical whether interactions occur within a single process, across Nodes, or between geographically distributed execution environments. Reliability guarantees, ordering, persistence, and recovery behavior shall be appropriate to the semantics of each primitive rather than uniformly applied to all communication.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Communication itself shall be observable. HAL shall monitor the health, performance, reliability, and operational characteristics of each communication primitive as part of its Self Model, enabling continuous evaluation and optimization of its own distributed behavior.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

