\fs36 \cf0 1. The Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 HAL is distributed, but it must still behave like one coherent authority.\
That creates a hard question:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 What happens when different parts of HAL hold different views of reality?
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
This will happen constantly.\
Examples:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls278\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Node reports that an Attempt is still running while the Execution Orchestrator believes its lease expired.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A resource reservation is visible to one subsystem but not yet another.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Provider reports success after HAL has already committed a replacement result.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A disconnected edge Node continues operating with stale policy.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A read model lags behind the authoritative event stream.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Two subsystems both believe they may modify the same state.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Replicas disagree after a partial failure.\
\ls278\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A network partition prevents immediate coordination.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 A weak architecture tries to keep every copy of state perfectly synchronized at all times.\
That usually produces either:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls279\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 intolerable latency,\
\ls279\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 brittle coupling,\
\ls279\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 or false confidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 HAL needs a more disciplined model.\
The real question is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 Which state must be strongly authoritative, which state may be eventually consistent, and how does HAL reconcile disagreement without losing truth or authority?
