\f6\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 \uc0\u9989 
\f0\b  Decision 24 \'97 Distributed State and Consistency Model (LOCKED)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 HAL shall use an authority-scoped consistency model in which every authoritative state domain has exactly one recognized owner responsible for validating, ordering, and committing state transitions within that domain. Replicas, projections, caches, indexes, and read models may distribute access to state but shall not acquire authority through replication.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b HAL shall distinguish authoritative state from derived state. Authoritative state shall determine what HAL recognizes as true and shall require durable, versioned, policy-valid mutation. Derived state shall remain rebuildable, replaceable, and non-authoritative regardless of its operational usefulness.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Authoritative entities shall use explicit versions, and state-changing Commands shall declare the version or authority context against which they were issued. Stale, conflicting, expired, or superseded mutations shall not overwrite current authoritative state.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Each authority shall preserve an immutable ordered history of accepted transitions sufficient to reconstruct its state. HAL shall require deterministic ordering within an authority domain but shall not impose a universal total order across unrelated domains. Cross-domain operations shall preserve causal references to the authoritative versions on which they depended.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b HAL shall support explicit read-consistency classes, including authoritative, monotonic, bounded-staleness, and eventual reads. Consumers shall declare the consistency level required by their decision, and higher-risk actions shall obtain current authoritative state rather than relying on stale projections.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b During network partitions or disconnection, subsystems shall preserve existing authority boundaries. Loss of connectivity shall not grant new authority. Nodes may continue only within explicit delegated envelopes defining scope, policy, budget, time, risk, and reconciliation obligations. Authority shall expire when delegation expires.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Conflicting or late state shall be resolved through authoritative ownership, version, causality, lease or fencing authority, policy, and domain-specific reconciliation. Last-write-wins semantics shall not be used for authoritative state unless explicitly proven safe for that domain. Rejected or superseded information shall remain preserved as evidence without becoming current truth.
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Authorities may create integrity-verified snapshots for recovery and performance, but snapshots shall remain derived from and anchored to the authoritative transition history. Schema evolution shall be versioned and replay-safe so that HAL can continue interpreting and reconstructing its historical state across system upgrades.
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
