\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Proposed Locked Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL shall maintain one authoritative Policy System responsible for the identity, definition, scope, precedence, versioning, lifecycle, amendment history, and authorized issuance of all machine-enforceable policy. Other subsystems and Nodes may evaluate policy but shall not independently redefine or acquire authority over it.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall distinguish policy from implementation logic. Policy shall govern what actions are permitted, prohibited, required, constrained, deferred, escalated, or conditioned. Authoritative policy shall remain identifiable, inspectable, versioned, and traceable rather than being hidden exclusively within subsystem code.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policies shall be organized into explicit authority layers, with constitutional policy highest, followed by Founder policy, delegated administrative policy, Objective policy, Plan policy, operational policy, user preference, and learned optimization. Lower layers may refine but shall not weaken or contradict higher-authority mandatory policy.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 HAL shall distinguish mandatory policies from advisory policies. Mandatory policy shall establish non-negotiable constraints and obligations. Advisory policy may influence optimization only within the space permitted by mandatory policy. Learned behavior and inferred preference shall remain advisory unless explicitly promoted through an authorized policy action.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policy evaluation shall be deterministic and reproducible. Every evaluation shall identify the policy bundle, input facts, evidence versions, authority context, and evaluation time used to produce the result. Hidden mutable inputs shall not determine consequential policy outcomes.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 The Policy System shall issue signed, immutable, versioned policy bundles that authorized subsystems and Nodes may evaluate locally. Distributed evaluation shall improve availability and latency without transferring policy authority. Bundles shall declare scope, validity, required inputs, integrity, and revocation behavior.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policy freshness requirements shall be explicit. High-risk actions may require current authoritative confirmation, while lower-risk actions may use bounded-staleness bundles. Revoked or expired policy authority shall not remain valid merely because a Node is disconnected.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policy conflicts shall be resolved through explicit authority, mandatory status, specificity, version, temporal validity, and authorized override rules. Unresolved conflicts among mandatory policies shall result in denial, deferral, or escalation rather than inferred permission.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Exceptions shall be represented as narrow, authorized, versioned policies with explicit scope, justification, duration, compensating controls, and audit obligations. Informal or implementation-level bypasses shall not constitute valid exceptions.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Consequential evaluations shall produce durable Policy Decision Records containing the requested action, actor, target, applicable policy versions, material evidence, conflicts, outcome, obligations, rationale, and evaluation time. Policy explanations shall identify the actual governing rules and shall not be reconstructed solely as post hoc narrative.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policy outcomes may attach enforceable obligations before, during, or after execution. The Execution Orchestrator and relevant authorities shall track satisfaction of those obligations, and an allowed action shall not be considered validly completed when its mandatory obligations remain unmet.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \

\f0\b \strokec2 Policy may restrict, reject, defer, or require replanning, but shall not silently redefine human intent. Changes to intended outcomes shall remain subject to planning and authority rather than being disguised as policy compliance.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
