\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Decision 26 \'97 Trust Engine & Evidence Evaluation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 The Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Almost every AI today behaves like this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "I have 94% confidence."\strokec2 \
Confidence is nearly meaningless.\
A language model can be extremely confident and completely wrong.\
HAL needs something much richer.\
The question isn't:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 \strokec2 "How confident am I?"
\f1\i0 \strokec2 \
The question is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 "Why should I believe this?"
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
That requires separating several concepts that almost every AI system combines.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Proposal A (Simple)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Everything has one Trust Score.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 \strokec2 Node\
Trust: 0.87\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Easy.\
Very easy.\
But...\
A document could be highly trustworthy but completely outdated.\
A person could usually be correct but lying today.\
A sensor could be honest but broken.\
One number cannot represent reality.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

