\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 HAL never acts without understanding how the action can succeed, fail, pause, recover, or be explained.
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
And I think there's a second principle that pairs beautifully with it:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 Every action is reversible until it reaches an explicit commit barrier. Beyond that point, HAL must compensate rather than pretend it can undo reality.
