\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Decision 51 \'97 Self-Description, Identity Continuity & Constitutional Self-Awareness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The fundamental question is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 How does HAL know what it is?
\f1\b0 \strokec2 \
Not philosophically.\
Architecturally.\
Today an LLM can answer:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 "Who are you?"\strokec2 \
because the prompt says so.\
Tomorrow...\
You swap models.\
Upgrade hardware.\
Replace every service.\
Migrate to new infrastructure.\
How does HAL still know it is HAL?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Three approaches\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Option A \'97 Prompt Identity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 "I am HAL."\
Stored inside prompts.\
Easy.\
Fragile.\
Lose the prompt.\
Identity disappears.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Option B \'97 Configuration Identity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Identity lives in configuration files.\
Better.\
Still too shallow.\
Configuration describes a system.\
It doesn't define identity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Option C \'97 Constitutional Self-Description (\strokec2 My Recommendation\strokec2 )\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 HAL maintains an explicit, governed model of itself.\
Not merely:\
"My name is HAL."\
Instead:\
"I am this constitutional system."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

